      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSituated in the peaceful countryside of Graigacurragh, Granagh, Kilmallock, Co. Limerick, this charming four-bedroom detached residence offers an excellent opportunity to acquire a well-maintained family home set on approximately 0.5 acres. Surrounded by beautiful countryside and enjoying picturesque rural views, the property combines the tranquillity of country living with the convenience of nearby amenities.\n\nThe home is accessed through a gated entrance and is complemented by mature gardens that create a private and welcoming setting. The generous rear garden provides an ideal space for families, gardening enthusiasts or those who simply wish to relax and enjoy the peaceful surroundings. Ample off-street parking is available, adding to the practicality of this attractive home.\n\nInternally, the property offers bright, comfortable accommodation with four well-proportioned bedrooms and spacious living areas suited to everyday family life. Heating is provided by an oil-fired central heating system, while a solid fuel stove with back boiler adds warmth, character and efficiency throughout the home.\n\nOutside, the property benefits from a detached garage along with a second storage shed, providing excellent additional space for storage, a workshop or a variety of other uses. These outbuildings further enhance the property's appeal and versatility.\n\nIdeally located, the property is within easy reach of Granagh village and a local primary school, while the renowned village of Adare is just a 12-minute drive away, offering an excellent range of shops, cafés, restaurants and other amenities. The surrounding area is renowned for its scenic countryside, woodland walks and outdoor recreational opportunities, making it an ideal location for those who appreciate nature and rural living.\n\nCombining comfortable family accommodation, generous outdoor space and a beautiful countryside setting, this delightful home presents an excellent opportunity for purchasers seeking a peaceful lifestyle without compromising on convenience. Viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this wonderful property has to offer.\n\nPorch 1.9 x 3.9 tiled\n\nLiving room 4.9 x 4.2 laminate flooring, stove with back boiler\n\nBedroom 2.9 x 2.7 carpet\n\nKitchen/dining room 3.1 x 7.1 tiled, fitted units, back door\n\nBedroom 5.3 x 2.5 carpet\n\nBedroom 2.6 x 4.5 carpet\n\nBathroom 2.8 x 1.8 tiled, electric shower\n\nBedroom 4.3 x 3.2 carpet\n\nKEY FEATURES:\n4 bed 1 bath\nDetached home\nOil fired central heating with back boiler stove\nMains water\nSeptic tank\nDetached garage\nSecond shed for storage\nSet on C. 0.5 acre site\nExpands to C. 120 sqm\nAmazing countryside views and setting\nOff street parking\nBuilt C. 1933\nD1 BER rating\n\nViewing is highly recommended.\nThese particulars have been prepared by DNG John Ryan and whilst every care has been taken to ensure that these are accurate and correct, we are not responsible for any errors, omissions, inaccuracies, if the property is let, sold or withdrawn from sale or if it is not suitable for your purpose. These particulars are for information only and are given under the strict understanding that they do not form part of any contract. Neither whole nor any part of this document or any reference thereto may be included in any public document, circular or statement nor published without the written consent of DNG John Ryan. PSL: 003615"
